1
00:01:37,239 --> 00:01:39,200
What are you up to?

2
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,159
Weren't you going to take Mrs. Lin's case?

3
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,439
Why did you suddenly change your mind

4
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:43,640
and go look for Liang Zidong?

5
00:01:45,719 --> 00:01:47,159
Where are we even driving to?

6
00:01:47,159 --> 00:01:49,760
Just follow the address on the navigation for now.

7
00:01:53,239 --> 00:01:54,040
Let me ask you something.

8
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:56,959
Doesn't Rujie occasionally

9
00:01:56,959 --> 00:01:59,480
get one of those crucial cases

10
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:00,280
that can directly impact

11
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:02,359
the firm's growth for the next 3-5 years?

12
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:03,920
I haven't been here long myself.

13
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:05,239
How would I know all that?

14
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:06,879
But I asked around.

15
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,439
This Liang Zidong case

16
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,159
is probably exactly what you mean.

17
00:02:12,479 --> 00:02:13,360
So that means

18
00:02:14,159 --> 00:02:15,639
whoever finds Liang Zidong

19
00:02:15,639 --> 00:02:17,400
will get to take this case,

20
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:19,960
and all the firm's future resources

21
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,719
will be focused on them, right?

22
00:02:21,919 --> 00:02:22,520
Right.

23
00:02:23,039 --> 00:02:25,280
And for a young lawyer,

24
00:02:25,919 --> 00:02:27,680
whoever manages to take this case

25
00:02:28,319 --> 00:02:30,360
can practically transform their career.

26
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,400
But so far,

27
00:02:35,919 --> 00:02:37,039
there's been zero progress.

28
00:02:42,319 --> 00:02:44,360
He's very likely to show up at a hospital.

29
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:45,879
A hospital?

30
00:02:48,639 --> 00:02:49,360
Why?

31
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,080
Earlier, when I was looking at

32
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,120
the video evidence Mrs. Lin gave me,

33
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:53,919
I noticed that

34
00:02:53,919 --> 00:02:56,439
Liang Zidong also appeared in the video.

35
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:58,280
And after I zoomed in on the footage,

36
00:02:58,280 --> 00:02:59,319
guess what I saw?

37
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:02,599
Liang Zidong injecting himself with insulin.

38
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,080
Hello.

39
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,039
Are you Liang Zidong's wife?

40
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,800
I'm Ding Ning from Rujie Law Firm.

41
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:30,439
The thing is,

42
00:03:30,719 --> 00:03:32,520
regarding your husband's case,

43
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,759
we have a few questions.

44
00:03:33,759 --> 00:03:35,199
Would you mind helping us out?

45
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,159
Does your husband regularly take insulin?

46
00:03:40,479 --> 00:03:42,159
How often does he get his medication?

47
00:03:42,159 --> 00:03:43,000
Do you mind telling me?

48
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,280
What brand is it?

49
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,879
And what's the dosage?

50
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:51,159
His insulin is a foreign brand.

51
00:03:51,319 --> 00:03:53,680
I checked every hospital and pharmacy,

52
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,159
and found that only this hospital

53
00:03:55,199 --> 00:03:56,680
has this brand of insulin.

54
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:59,439
Plus, per his medical insurance records,

55
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:01,400
counting back from his last refill,

56
00:04:01,879 --> 00:04:03,520
his medication is almost out.

57
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:05,240
Which means,

58
00:04:06,159 --> 00:04:08,120
no matter where Liang Zidong is kept,

59
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,479
for his health,

60
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,120
they will have to bring Liang Zidong

61
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,240
here to buy insulin.

62
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,520
Then we just have to lie in wait.

63
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,439
If we stake out the hospital for two days,

64
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:20,040
we might just catch him.

65
00:04:20,879 --> 00:04:22,040
How did you find that out?

66
00:04:23,399 --> 00:04:25,120
Just had to ask the medicine scalpers.

67
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,519
Impressive, Ding Ning.

68
00:04:29,199 --> 00:04:30,639
Let's see if we can catch him then.

69
00:04:30,639 --> 00:04:32,720
I'll go talk to the Security Office soon

70
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,879
to pull two days of surveillance footage.

71
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,480
What are these two kids doing?

72
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,079
Jumping on a trampoline.

73
00:04:47,399 --> 00:04:47,959
What?

74
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:49,120
Jumping on a trampoline.

75
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,319
A trampoline?

76
00:04:50,759 --> 00:04:53,639
Awu is amazing at the trampoline!

77
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,000
You've made a lot of new friends, right?

78
00:05:00,279 --> 00:05:00,959
Awu...

79
00:05:00,959 --> 00:05:03,439
Grandpa has to go out. I'll be back later.

80
00:05:04,079 --> 00:05:05,360
Can you take care of yourself?

81
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,079
Okay.

82
00:05:08,079 --> 00:05:08,680
Okay.

83
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:09,399
All right.

84
00:05:10,199 --> 00:05:12,480
I'll bring you some treats later, okay?

85
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,439
Be good.

86
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,120
You're here.

87
00:05:52,199 --> 00:05:53,040
Want to go for a walk?

88
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,000
Careful, don't scratch it.

89
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:07,720
Here we go.

90
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,319
My dad built all these buildings here too.

91
00:06:18,639 --> 00:06:20,000
Your dad is amazing.

92
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,240
Let's go. I'll show you around.

93
00:06:31,199 --> 00:06:31,800
Close the door.

94
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,639
Easy, easy.

95
00:06:39,639 --> 00:06:41,120
What do you think this family does?

96
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,160
Don't take other people's things.

97
00:07:10,879 --> 00:07:12,800
Think they were just lying here like this?

98
00:07:40,399 --> 00:07:41,199
Someone's coming.

99
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,040
Let's go!

100
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:04,480
Why isn't he talking?

101
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:09,480
He can't speak.

102
00:08:10,399 --> 00:08:11,519
And he can't stand up either.

103
00:08:16,519 --> 00:08:17,480
Do you know him?

104
00:08:18,519 --> 00:08:19,399
No, I don't.

105
00:08:21,399 --> 00:08:23,480
I have someone like this at home too.

106
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,960
Let's take him out to play.

107
00:09:11,919 --> 00:09:12,799
Be careful.

108
00:09:12,799 --> 00:09:13,559
Don't drop it.

109
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,080
Let's go back.

110
00:09:35,519 --> 00:09:36,879
Otherwise, his family will worry.

111
00:09:46,799 --> 00:09:48,759
Why do all these buildings look the same?

112
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,120
I don't think it's this one.

113
00:09:53,879 --> 00:09:54,879
It must be that one.

114
00:09:57,399 --> 00:09:59,200
Grandpa, do you remember your home?

115
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:10,559
It's over. We can't find his home.

116
00:10:17,159 --> 00:10:20,480
This will help grandpa find his home.

117
00:10:20,559 --> 00:10:21,559
Definitely.

118
00:10:21,799 --> 00:10:23,320
It's way better than us searching blindly.

119
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,120
Ready.

120
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:28,279
Three, two, one.

121
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,200
Go!

122
00:10:35,279 --> 00:10:36,039
Wait a minute.

123
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:51,240
Ready. Three, two, one.

124
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:52,159
Go.

125
00:10:56,919 --> 00:10:58,200
Stop looking. Let's go.

126
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,480
Hurry up.

127
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,159
Hurry, hurry!

128
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:15,759
Sir, why are you here all alone?

129
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:17,120
Where is your family?

130
00:11:19,399 --> 00:11:21,159
Grandpa, who brought you here?

131
00:12:57,919 --> 00:12:59,600
Why are you back so late too?

132
00:13:06,679 --> 00:13:07,440
What's wrong?

133
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:13,279
A few days ago,

134
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:17,399
someone passed away.

135
00:13:20,159 --> 00:13:22,320
I had to send him for cremation.

136
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,639
These are his gold tooth and stones.

137
00:13:25,759 --> 00:13:26,919
See how you want to handle them.

138
00:13:41,039 --> 00:13:41,919
So it turns out,

139
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:47,000
a person can eventually turn into ashes,

140
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,320
and then they just

141
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:53,559
put it in a little box.

142
00:13:58,039 --> 00:13:59,120
The strange thing is,

143
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,960
I really didn't feel anything.

144
00:14:05,879 --> 00:14:07,559
Was that person your friend?

145
00:14:11,039 --> 00:14:11,840
Not really.

146
00:14:14,159 --> 00:14:18,120
But compared to so-called friends,

147
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:21,440
we were a bit more complicated.

148
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:27,840
You've been writing to me all these years.

149
00:14:29,279 --> 00:14:30,159
Why?

150
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,399
Because I hate you.

151
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:41,000
I didn't want you to move on so easily.

152
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:45,000
Think you're the only one in prison?

153
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,240
I've been in one too.

154
00:14:56,159 --> 00:14:57,840
Then I actually felt relieved.

155
00:14:59,799 --> 00:15:02,519
I was wondering why I'd feel relieved.

156
00:15:02,519 --> 00:15:03,919
Maybe I'm just afraid that

157
00:15:06,519 --> 00:15:07,919
now that he's free,

158
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:13,080
everything between us

159
00:15:14,399 --> 00:15:16,039
just went away with him.

160
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:21,320
The once-unforgettable memories

161
00:15:22,879 --> 00:15:26,039
are fading away bit by bit.

162
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:32,759
Afraid of what?

163
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:35,720
I don't know.

164
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,720
What about you?

165
00:15:39,879 --> 00:15:41,000
Why are you up so late?

166
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:47,240
Endless things to do.

167
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,960
Then go back to your room and sleep.

168
00:16:07,519 --> 00:16:09,679
Also helping Zhao Yijie find Liang Zidong?

169
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,919
The other day when we had dumplings,

170
00:16:15,919 --> 00:16:17,200
I noticed the paper under our plates

171
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,799
had the Fuxia Group logo on it.

172
00:16:19,159 --> 00:16:21,159
And so did the paper you just threw away.

173
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,759
May I speak frankly?

174
00:16:26,159 --> 00:16:26,879
Go ahead.

175
00:16:27,639 --> 00:16:28,879
I just wanted to say,

176
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,519
Zhao Yijie adopted Yang A'wu,

177
00:16:31,759 --> 00:16:33,519
but it's like you adopted him.

178
00:16:34,039 --> 00:16:36,200
The kid is here with you most of the time.

179
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:37,360
Even with Rujie's affairs,

180
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,320
he asks for your help day and night.

181
00:16:39,679 --> 00:16:41,200
I know it's not my place to say this,

182
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,879
but isn't he taking a mile

183
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,559
when you give him an inch?

184
00:16:45,279 --> 00:16:47,120
Besides, the kid is going to grow up.

185
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:50,080
What if one day, when the time comes,

186
00:16:50,399 --> 00:16:51,440
Zhao Yijie, for Yang's sake...

187
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:52,639
Ding Ning, what if...

188
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:55,080
Just hypothetically, what if

189
00:16:57,159 --> 00:16:59,120
something happens to Zhao Yijie and me,

190
00:17:00,559 --> 00:17:02,120
would you adopt Yang A'wu?

191
00:17:12,559 --> 00:17:13,279
Hello, Zhou Hao.

192
00:17:13,279 --> 00:17:15,000
I found them. Come quickly.

193
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,359
What's the situation?

194
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:22,400
They're right inside.

195
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:23,640
Which room is Liang Zidong in?

196
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,839
It's all up to you now.

197
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,279
I'll back you up from out here.

198
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:27,480
Alright.

199
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:29,279
Keep an eye on your phone.

200
00:17:29,279 --> 00:17:29,960
Okay.

201
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,480
Just a second.

202
00:17:54,519 --> 00:17:55,720
The Deposit will go back to your account.

203
00:17:55,839 --> 00:17:56,680
Thank you.

204
00:18:04,279 --> 00:18:05,000
Hello.

205
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,720
Hello. Do you have any rooms available?

206
00:18:06,839 --> 00:18:07,519
Yes, we do.

207
00:18:07,519 --> 00:18:09,720
Need a Standard room or a Deluxe room?

208
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:10,880
So, here's the thing.

209
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,079
Our company is having a team building.

210
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,440
We're thinking of next week,

211
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,559
and we'll probably need 7 or 8 rooms.

212
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:17,039
And, well...

213
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:19,319
our boss is a little superstitious.

214
00:18:19,519 --> 00:18:20,680
He wants the sixth floor.

215
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,119
For good luck, you know.

216
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,279
I'm sorry.

217
00:18:23,279 --> 00:18:25,400
We've already leased out the 6th floor.

218
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,880
There are no vacant rooms at the moment.

219
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,480
I see.

220
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,519
How about this?

221
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,039
We still have rooms on the fifth floor.

222
00:18:32,039 --> 00:18:33,880
The layout is identical to the 6th floor.

223
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,799
Let me show you.

224
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:37,000
The fifth floor...

225
00:18:37,319 --> 00:18:38,119
That works too.

226
00:18:38,359 --> 00:18:39,400
Okay, please wait a moment.

227
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:39,839
Okay.

228
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:46,559
This way.

229
00:18:48,559 --> 00:18:50,319
Hello, I'd like a room.

230
00:18:50,759 --> 00:18:51,559
I have a reservation.

231
00:18:51,799 --> 00:18:53,279
Okay, please wait a moment then.

232
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:54,759
Alright, how about I head up first?

233
00:18:54,839 --> 00:18:55,559
Okay.

234
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:01,519
Hello.

235
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:14,599
Zhou Hao,

236
00:20:15,319 --> 00:20:16,920
Liang Zidong is in 601.

237
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,640
Call Zhao Yijie right now.

238
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:19,440
Tell him to hurry over.

239
00:20:20,279 --> 00:20:21,039
Bye.

240
00:20:39,559 --> 00:20:40,319
What are you doing?

241
00:20:46,519 --> 00:20:48,160
I'm Ding Ning, Liang Zidong's legal counsel.

242
00:20:48,319 --> 00:20:50,559
During his residential surveillance,

243
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:51,799
I invoke the Right to meet with client.

244
00:20:58,839 --> 00:21:00,000
If within three minutes,

245
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,039
I don't message my partner downstairs,

246
00:21:02,359 --> 00:21:03,319
he will be certain

247
00:21:03,319 --> 00:21:05,039
you're stopping me from seeing Mr. Liang.

248
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,240
Then my partner will immediately

249
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,000
send a Complaint letter to the Bureau of Justice.

250
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:08,920
That way, even if you

251
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:10,720
get any evidence out of him in that room,

252
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:12,640
I can use this to petition the court

253
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,799
for the Exclusionary rule.

254
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,519
Making your interrogation useless.

255
00:21:15,799 --> 00:21:17,279
You're a lawyer just because you say so?

256
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:18,720
The Representation Agreement and paperwork

257
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:19,839
are in my phone.

258
00:21:20,039 --> 00:21:21,480
Your inefficiency leaves you with

259
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:23,400
only one minute left to hesitate.

260
00:21:27,559 --> 00:21:28,480
Oops, how careless.

261
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,599
The phone screen is completely shattered.

262
00:21:36,079 --> 00:21:37,920
Guess we can't verify your identity now.

263
00:21:39,519 --> 00:21:41,640
That's fine. I'm meticulous.

264
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,559
Should we notify the Captain?

265
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:56,000
Meeting my client alone is my right.

266
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:57,160
You have no right to sit in.

267
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:04,960
Mr. Liang.

268
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,880
I am your legal counsel, Ding Ning.

269
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:10,480
Great. They finally sent me a lawyer.

270
00:22:10,799 --> 00:22:11,559
Hello, hello.

271
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:12,440
Well...

272
00:22:13,119 --> 00:22:13,920
There are police outside.

273
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:14,839
Did they give you a hard time?

274
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:15,519
Come, have a seat.

275
00:22:15,519 --> 00:22:16,160
I'm fine.

276
00:22:16,839 --> 00:22:18,240
The whole law firm was looking for you.

277
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:19,960
I never expected

278
00:22:20,359 --> 00:22:21,880
this place to be so close to Rujie.

279
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,000
You're from Rujie?

280
00:22:29,559 --> 00:22:30,880
Zhao Yijie sent you?

281
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:33,799
Yes. You'll be able to go home soon

282
00:22:33,799 --> 00:22:35,079
and reunite with your family.

283
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:39,240
